  "weeklyExtras": {
    "week": 8,
    "tagline": "Week 8 News · Division Wars · Bad Luck · Big Names · Week 9 Smoke",
    "kicker": "GFL Insider · Week 8",
    "headline": "THE WILD WEST HAS A KING. THE EAST HAS BEASTS. THE CENTRAL HAS CHAOS.",
    "deck": "Redwood keeps stacking wins without blowing anybody away, Sullco grabbed the East by the throat, Ticklesh!ts came roaring back from the dead, and Flint somehow turned another winning-caliber score into another loss. Eight weeks in, the standings are telling only half the story.",
    "story": [
      "Redwood Murder is sitting on top of the GFL at 7-1, but this is no spotless empire. Redwood survived Off Boys 94.24-87.06 while finishing ninth in Week 8 scoring. That has become the Redwood trick: stay alive, let the other guy blink, and walk out with the win. The Murder is #8 in points and #6 in all-play, yet nobody has been better at turning ordinary Sundays into victories. Call it luck if you want. At 7-1, Collin can call it first place.",
      "Out East, the MethMouths are starting to look less like a contender and more like the division's resident monster. Sullco dropped California 101.86-93.48 to reach 6-2, with a season profile that backs up the record: #2 in scoring and #2 in all-play. Behind Owen, things are getting feral. Simpson Sith and Your Mom are both 4-4, and Your Mom just hung 123.22 on Eskimo Brothers. The Beasts of the East have six weeks left to start eating each other.",
      "Then there is the Central, where normal football apparently goes to die. One week after collapsing to 68.08, Turbulent Ticklesh!ts detonated for 127.46, the Week 8 high, and moved to 5-3. Medford shocked Simpson Sith with 121.00. Flint scored 118.08, the third-highest total of the entire league, and lost anyway. The Central produced the week's three biggest scores, yet two of those teams entered the week buried near the bottom of the standings. Chaos is not a side effect there. It is the division identity.",
      "The player trail makes the personalities even clearer. Jaxon Smith-Njigba has landed in Simpson Sith's ESPN-listed Top 3 in seven of eight weeks, the same frequency Joe Burrow has carried California's weekly leaderboard. Jahmyr Gibbs has been an Off Boys Top-3 fixture six times. James Cook III has done it six times for Space Cadets, Christian McCaffrey six times for Barton, and Kenneth Walker III six times for Ticklesh!ts. These are not just good players. Through eight weeks, they are the fingerprints their teams keep leaving at the scene.",
      "And then there is Flint. Stephen Davis is 1-7 with the #6 scoring offense and a perfectly even 44-44 all-play record. That is not a normal last-place team; it is a team that keeps arriving at the casino with a decent hand and watching the dealer pull twenty-one. Week 8 was the cleanest example yet: 118.08 points, third-best in the league, zero wins added to the standings. If regression ever comes to collect its debt, Flint would like the address."
    ],
    "awards": [
      {
        "emoji": "🔥",
        "title": "Back From the Dead",
        "team": "Turbulent Ticklesh!ts",
        "detail": "From 68.08 in Week 7 to a league-best 127.46 in Week 8, a 59.38-point resurrection. Tyler went from the basement to the penthouse in seven days."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "⛰️",
        "title": "Mountain Warning",
        "team": "Medford MountainMen",
        "detail": "121.00 points and an upset of Simpson Sith. The 2-6 record still looks ugly, but 106.85 per game over the last three says Doug is no longer an easy out."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "💔",
        "title": "Cruel and Unusual Punishment",
        "team": "Flint Tropics",
        "detail": "118.08 was the third-best score of Week 8 and bought Stephen absolutely nothing. At 1-7 with the #6 PF profile, the Tropics remain the league’s patron saint of bad timing."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "🚀",
        "title": "Medallion Massacre",
        "team": "Space Cadets",
        "detail": "97.30-57.38 over Barton in the Gonzo/Dawg Medallion game. The 39.92-point margin was Week 8’s widest, and Kris did it without even reaching 100."
      },
      {
        "emoji": "🧬",
        "title": "The Sith Signature",
        "team": "Simpson Sith",
        "detail": "Jaxon Smith-Njigba has appeared in Danny’s ESPN-listed Top 3 in seven of eight weeks. If Simpson Sith has a calling card this season, JSN keeps signing it."
      }
    ],
    "tidbits": [
      "Redwood is 7-1 with only the #8 scoring total and #6 all-play record. That is less steamroller than escape artist, but seven escapes still count as seven wins.",
      "Ticklesh!ts owns the league’s #1 PF and #1 all-play marks at 5-3. If the standings are the résumé, Tyler’s underlying numbers are the glowing recommendation letter.",
      "California is 6-2 while sitting #9 in PF and #10 in all-play. Tavis has banked the wins, but the West is getting dangerous if the scoring does not wake back up.",
      "Off Boys is 3-5 despite ranking #5 in PF and #4 in all-play. Kyle’s record says fringe team; the weekly field says this is exactly the kind of team nobody wants catching a break.",
      "Flint is 1-7 with the #6 PF total and a 44-44 all-play record. The Tropics are not being beaten like a 1-7 team; they are losing like one anyway.",
      "Jaxon Smith-Njigba and Joe Burrow have each appeared in their team’s ESPN-listed Top 3 seven times in eight weeks. Simpson and California have different records, but both have a very obvious engine.",
      "Jahmyr Gibbs has six Top-3 appearances for Off Boys. Kyle may be 3-5, but Gibbs keeps giving the offense a pulse even when the standings refuse to cooperate.",
      "Christian McCaffrey has six Top-3 appearances for Barton, but Week 8 ended without him among the displayed three as the Spartans cratered to 57.38. When the franchise centerpiece disappears from the weekly leaderboard, Barton has very little room for error.",
      "Week 8’s three highest scores belonged to Ticklesh!ts, Medford, and Flint. Welcome to the Central: one division leader, two losing records, and all of the week’s heavy artillery.",
      "Barton’s 57.38 is the lowest score through eight weeks, slipping below Medford’s 58.08 in Week 4. Matt did not just lose the Medallion; he left his name on the wrong side of the season record book."
    ],
    "playoffTitle": "Six Weeks Left · Nobody Gets Comfortable",
    "playoffInsights": [
      "East — Sullco is 6-2 with the scoring muscle to match. Simpson and Your Mom sit at 4-4, and Your Mom is heating up. Owen has the lead, but this division has teeth behind him.",
      "West — Redwood’s 7-1 record owns the headline, California sits one game back at 6-2, and Eskimo Brothers lurks at 5-3. The Wild West is officially a three-horse race, with Off Boys carrying spoiler numbers that look much better than 3-5.",
