    "lookingAhead": "WEEK 9: SIX GAMES, SIX DIFFERENT KINDS OF TROUBLE. Off Boys vs. Sullco MethMouths — The 3-5 team with #5 PF and #4 all-play gets a shot at the 6-2 Beast of the East. If Kyle wants the standings to start respecting the numbers, beating Owen would be a loud way to ask. Simpson Sith vs. Redwood Murder — The Original Members game. Danny owns the league’s all-time wins record; Collin brings the 7-1 record and the league’s best escape act. Simpson’s #3 PF/#3 all-play profile says this is anything but a friendly reunion. Turbulent Ticklesh!ts vs. Space Cadets — Tyler brings the league’s #1 PF/#1 all-play machine; Kris brings a two-wins-in-three-weeks surge and a freshly polished Gonzo/Dawg Medallion. Ceiling meets momentum. Medford MountainMen vs. Your Mom — Two teams whose recent scoring looks far nastier than their records. Medford just dropped 121.00; Your Mom carries a 111.31 last-three average. Somebody’s heater survives. California Un-Named Team vs. Eskimo Brothers — Here comes the West knife fight. California has the 6-2 record, Sean has the stronger scoring profile, and one result could turn Redwood’s comfortable-looking lead into a much noisier neighborhood. THE Barton Spartans vs. Flint Tropics — The Desperation Bowl. Barton comes off the season’s lowest score; Flint comes off yet another good score with nothing to show for it. Somebody gets relief. Somebody gets a longer week."
